Brand the web Getting Started walkthrough.

The welcome page's featured walkthrough is the one piece of product naming
that lives in source strings rather than product.json: on first launch the
user is greeted with "Get Started with VS Code for the Web" over a page
titled "Setup VS Code Web". The pre-pivot build rewrote both strings in the
packaged nls.messages files; that mutation lost its home when the download
script was deleted, so every Code - OSS build since has shipped Microsoft's
naming on the very first screen a user reads.

The walkthrough's telemetry footer needs no equivalent edit: upstream gates
it on productService.enableTelemetry, which the branding overlay sets to
false, so it never renders here.

--- a/src/vs/workbench/contrib/welcomeGettingStarted/common/gettingStartedContent.ts
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/contrib/welcomeGettingStarted/common/gettingStartedContent.ts
@@ -289,12 +289,12 @@
